INT. STALLED ELEVATOR - DAY

Four people, mirrored walls, a dead floor indicator. Muzak plays softly.

WINIFRED, 50s, in a pantsuit, holds a cake box. LEOPOLD, 30s, in a delivery uniform, holds a balloon bouquet. DANIKA, 20s, in a bridesmaid dress, holds a phone with no signal. VIJAY, 40s, in a tux, holds nothing but a ring box.

Everyone smiles tightly.

WINIFRED
(to the group)
It's fine. It's a minor delay.

DANIKA
(to Vijay)
You're the groom?

VIJAY
Best man.

DANIKA
Where's the ring?

VIJAY
(to himself)
In the box. It's in the box. It's in the box.

The intercom crackles.

MAINTENANCE (V.O.)
Hello in there? Is anyone in the elevator?

LEOPOLD
Four of us!

MAINTENANCE (V.O.)
Great. Quick question. Do any of you have a wedding to be at?

All four stare at one another.

WINIFRED
(to the group)
Why do you ask?

MAINTENANCE (V.O.)
Because the groom just called. He says the bride's mother is stuck in an elevator with a cake, the best man, and a bridesmaid, and a balloon guy.

Winifred closes her eyes.

WINIFRED
(quietly)
I am the mother.

Vijay opens the ring box. It's empty.

VIJAY
(to himself)
Okay.
